      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-001-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Member States, industry, other stakeholders and WHO to implement a global approach to pandemic influenza preparedness \nand response. The key goals include: to improve and strengthen the sharing of influenza viruses with human pandemic \npotential through the WHO Global Influenza Surveillance and Response System (GISRS), and to increase the access of \ndeveloping countries to vaccines and other pandemic response supplies.\nThe Framework includes a benefit-sharing mechanism called the Partnership Contribution (PC). The PC is collected as an annual \ncash contribution from influenza vaccine, diagnost",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the Pandemic Influenza Preparedness Framework, which aims to improve sharing of influenza viruses with pandemic potential through WHO's GISRS network and to widen developing countries' access to vaccines and other supplies. It explains the Partnership Contribution, an annual payment by manufacturers that use GISRS, and how it funds preparedness capacity building, pandemic response and the PIP Secretariat, and thanks the staff who carry out the work.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
